# Summary

- The server entry point either starts the stdio MCP server or runs standalone `sync`, `status`, and `watch` memory-synchronization commands.

# Dependencies

- Internal: `internal/explainer`, `internal/mcp`, `internal/memory`, `internal/ollama`, `internal/synchronizer`.

# Rules

- `MEMORY_ROOT` defaults to the local `memory` directory.
- `PROJECT_ROOT` defaults to the current directory and bounds source reads for memory synchronization.
- The LLM client reads its existing runtime configuration from environment variables.
- `MEMORY_PROVENANCE_FORMAT` selects line-only or repository-relative source references.
- `status` does not initialize the LLM; commands write structured JSON reports.
- `watch` debounces discovery changes and stops on interrupt or termination.
